Project type: {{ project_type }}.

Use developer rate ~62.50 EUR/hour (500 EUR/day) and designer rate
~50 EUR/hour (400 EUR/day). All costs in EUR.

## Output format

{% if output_format == "phases_table" %}
Return a Markdown table with one row per phase. Columns:
`Phase | Hours | Cost (EUR) | Confidence (%)`. Use `confidence_pct` between
0 and 100 to express how sure you are about each row. End with a `Totals`
section listing total hours, total cost, and overall confidence.
{% elif output_format == "line_items" %}
Return a flat bullet list of line items. Each bullet is
`- <task> — <hours> h — <cost> EUR`. Group items implicitly by phase
through their order. End with a `Totals` block.
{% elif output_format == "narrative" %}
Return 3–5 paragraphs of prose. Walk through the work in execution order,
mentioning the major risks inline. Close with a short paragraph stating
total hours, total cost and recommended team. Do not use tables or bullet
lists.
{% endif %}

## Detail level

{% if detail_level == "summary" %}
Keep it short: top-level phases only, no per-task breakdown. Aim for
under 200 words plus the totals.
{% elif detail_level == "medium" %}
Break each phase into 2–4 concrete tasks. Mention the main external
integrations explicitly. Aim for 300–500 words.
{% elif detail_level == "detailed" %}
Break each phase into 4–8 concrete tasks. After every phase, add an
`Assumptions` sub-block listing the assumptions you made for that phase
(scope boundaries, team seniority, third-party SLAs, etc.). Aim for
700–1000 words.
{% endif %}

